LQG spin network → H₂⁺ and H₂ binding, as kernel-checked modules.
Root 70bb4035f70b8317e56678c55588f035419d5e31dffb70f31e097b0c5caab426 (./hyperactive take).
Relational, finite: charge networks carry integer labels; every quantity exact rational or exact algebraic. Gravitational input: Thiemann QSD V (gr-qc/9705019) operators on the spin network.

linkhop — electron hop on one link = 2×2 orthogonal matrix (entries −1/2, √3/2), from bholonomy's hop-amp. Levels ±1.

vertexhop — hop out of a 4-valent vertex along each link. Moving the electron's ½ to the other link-pair has coefficient +1 (6j with a zero entry = Racah's sum); per-link squared amplitudes sum to 1.

nethop — all-½ net: hop to a neighbour sends the link ½→1 two ways (by the neighbour's inner label), squared amplitudes 1/4 and 3/4, sum 1. Summed over the outcome: unit-amplitude walk. Hop amplitude t is one number for the whole net.

cover — the hop carries the link's U(1) holonomy, so it moves the link flux by 1. Electron + its flux = one walker on the graph's maximal abelian cover; two walks coincide iff their flux chains agree. Gauss's law holds after every walk (hexagon, smallest cage). Σn² is a potential on the cover.

fluxsplit — Σn² = Σh² + Σ(n−h)². Σh² = the charges' Coulomb part (field-energy = resistance-metric energy). n−h ranges over one coset of the integer circulations = the charges' class in the graph's abelian group (order = spanning-tree count). Electric term alone: energy between two charges = the shorter arc (a string). Foster's theorem checked on hexagon, cage, complete graph.

sectors — QSD V magnetic loops move no flux between vertices (625 sectors). Vertex energy is a function of the vertex charge only ⇒ the local terms carry no force between charges at different vertices.

netpiece — diamond net closed at period 2 = the 4-cube graph (16 vertices). Charge energy at separation 1–4: 15/32, 7/12, 61/96, 2/3. Kirchhoff over the rationals.

ringatom, netatom — H = (λ/2)·fluxenergy − t·hop − K·ringloops on the cover; moments at the nucleus = polynomial identities in t, K, λ.

ringbound — ring, exact: (λ/2)R − 2t ≤ E₀ ≤ (λ/2)R, R = eff-resistance = d(N−d)/N (checked, all rings ≤ 8). Lower bound without the dual-torus argument.

cwbound — net, free t and λ: discrete Collatz–Wielandt, min_u (Hψ)_u/ψ_u ≤ E₀ ≤ max_u (Hψ)_u/ψ_u. Potential and degree extremes checked ⇒ finite bracket on the bond depth.

H₂⁺ (net charge ⇒ a wall terminates the field):
h2plus-net — potentials checked against Kirchhoff at every vertex. t = 0: electron on a nucleus, that site neutral, energy independent of separation (no force). 2nd order in t: the shared-neighbour placement gains more than the opposite placement.
bondpoly — opposite-placement operator's characteristic polynomial is exactly p_f = x(x−118)(x−140) − s(6x−280), s = (280t/λ′)². Energy = least root of p_f.
bondsep, bondcross — shared-neighbour strictly lower for t/λ′ = 0 … 0.19, integer root-bracketing certificate, no crossover in the controlled regime. (Earlier large-t claim was false, withdrawn.)

H₂ (neutral ⇒ closed, no wall):
h2-net — electrostatic ground = two neutral atoms (energy 0 at any separation); every charge-separated config positive; binding is not electrostatic; the shared bond vertex admits only the spin singlet.
h2two — H₂ binds for every t > 0. Separated-atom state: Coulomb 0, diagonal 0 (no hop without leaving a proton); four one-hop neighbours each 3/4; the 2×2 [[0, −2t], [−2t, 3λ′/4]] has determinant −4t² < 0, lowest eigenvalue < 0. Binding = the hop.

Couplings: t (fixed by geometry) and K/λ. QSD V Maxwell Hamiltonian q_ab/(2Q²√q)[E²+B²], canonical pair (A, E/Q²): integer labels are fluxes of E/Q², so E = Q²·n, λ ∝ Q² ∝ α, K ∝ 1/Q² ∝ 1/α. K/λ = c_geom/α².
cgeom — c_geom = −3/8. Electric cost a − b = ¼·3^{1/4}(1−5^{1/4})²; magnetic self-term K₀₀ = −(3/32)·3^{1/4}(1−5^{1/4})². Common radical cancels: K₀₀/(a−b) = −3/8. Checked as 8·K₀₀ + 3·(a−b) = 0.
Universal, spectrum-independent: a − b = −2(K̄₀₀ − K̄₀₁) and K̄₀₀ + 3K̄₀₁ = 0 (four edges equivalent, tetrahedral angle K₀₁/K₀₀ = −1/3) ⇒ a − b = −(8/3)K̄₀₀ ⇒ −3/8. Holds at any symmetric 4-valent vertex.

Not pinned: the dimensionful prefactor of K/λ (ℓ_p powers, QSD V regularization constants) — no numeric K/λ until read off QSD V. α is a matter-action input, not predicted.

